=== tests/browser-smoke.py ===
PASS production scripts connect and render actual GFX packets without errors
PASS real pointer hold opens remote with no underlying click
PASS real short click sends exactly one atomic click
PASS held remote key repeats and stops on pointer release
PASS SageTV Options remains distinct from local hold menu
PASS keyboard text delivered literally as UTF-8 POST
PASS Guide click adds SELECT assist after native click
PASS right-hold setting opens remote without native context menu
PASS drag sends release but never activation click
PASS render-only view fits logical 16:9 canvas and Escape restores toolbar
PASS mobile remote fits viewport without horizontal clipping
PASS dark SageTV CLEAR_RECT reveals active video instead of covering it black
PASS menu remains opaque while color-key preview moves/resizes underlying video
PASS negative texture dimensions do not mirror text or erase surrounding menu
PASS no browser JavaScript exceptions throughout gestures/settings
Chromium browser smoke: 15 tests PASS (offline mocked transport; not live playback)
=== tests/browser-layout-smoke.py ===
PASS 1912x800 window uses full area below toolbar with all four GFX corners visible
PASS initial server connection receives the actual usable UI dimensions
PASS desktop, portrait, landscape and large windows resize without clipping or page overflow
PASS window changes send real resize API requests and redraw at the new native size
PASS image handle allocated only at connection remains valid after four native resizes
PASS fixed 720p option contains the entire 16:9 UI rather than zooming/cropping
PASS bottom-right pointer clicks map to the new native coordinates
PASS render-only view and toolbar restoration renegotiate usable height
PASS fullscreen entry and exit preserve the complete native drawing surface
PASS video startup/control and reserve promotion do not wait behind a blocked GFX image decode
PASS large GFX batch yields to browser tasks before completion while preserving draw order
PASS no JavaScript exceptions in auto-resize, cache reuse or independent media scheduling
Chromium layout/scheduling: 12 tests PASS (mock native transport, no live SageMC/video)
